<title>USA: Sri Lanka buys 100,000T optional wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka buys 100,000T optional wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka bought 100,000 tonnes of optional-origin wheat Friday for September and October shipment, U.S. exporters said.</p>
<p>The deal included 50,000 tonnes of soft wheat for September shipment and 50,000 of hard wheat for October. Because of high U.S. prices, exporters said they doubt the United States will supply the hard wheat, but could provide the soft wheat.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720--</p>
